---
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DemoFrame from '../components/DemoFrame.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'

const selectiveImport = `import '@caderno-ui/elements/card'

// Only add artwork when this screen actually uses it.
import '@caderno-ui/elements/icon'`
---

<DocsLayout
  description="The composition, dependency, and bundle boundaries used across Caderno UI."
  title="Composition"
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
    <h1>Small behavior, explicit composition.</h1>
    <p>
      Caderno UI separates semantic behavior from product content and optional
      artwork. The result is a source-owned API in the spirit of compositional
      systems, while the canonical Lit implementation remains framework
      agnostic.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="rules-title">
    <h2 id="rules-title">The review criteria</h2>
    <div class="rules-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Compound when hierarchy varies</h3>
        <p>
          Card and Tabs expose named structural primitives because applications
          need to reorder, omit, or enrich those regions.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Slots when content varies</h3>
        <p>
          Button adornments, Input prefixes, and Callout illustrations are
          slots. A string prop must not pull another visual package into a
          bundle.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Own behavior when semantics depend on it</h3>
        <p>
          Modal owns its dialog and focus lifecycle; Alert owns live-region and
          dismissal behavior; form controls own native validation.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Keep intrinsic marks internal</h3>
        <p>
          Close, check, direction, and status marks are tiny internal SVGs.
          Product-facing doodles remain an explicit <code>cad-icon</code> import.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <DemoFrame
    title="Composition without hidden dependencies"
    description="The Card entrypoint works alone; the application opts into Badge and Icon for this particular presentation."
  >
    <cad-card tone="blue">
      <cad-card-header>
        <cad-card-kicker>Bundle boundary</cad-card-kicker>
        <cad-card-title><h2>Review search delivery</h2></cad-card-title>
      </cad-card-header>
      <cad-card-content>
        <p>
          The surface, hierarchy, status label, and doodle come from separate
          public entrypoints and can be shipped independently.
        </p>
      </cad-card-content>
      <cad-card-footer>
        <cad-badge tone="mint">Verified</cad-badge>
      </cad-card-footer>
    </cad-card>
  </DemoFrame>

  <CodeBlock code={selectiveImport} language="ts" />

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="delivery-title">
    <h2 id="delivery-title">Enforced in CI</h2>
    <p>
      Every public Elements and React entrypoint has its own gzip budget. Static
      checks reject primitive components that import the public icon registry,
      and bundle inspection rejects Rough.js anywhere outside Chart.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .rules-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 18rem), 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .rules-grid article {
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
      background: var(--cad-surface-raised);
      border: 1px dashed var(--cad-line-strong);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
    }

    .rules-grid :is(h3, p) {
      margin-block: 0;
    }

    .rules-grid p {
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
    }

    cad-card {
      max-width: 36rem;
    }
  </style>
</DocsLayout>

<script>
  import '@caderno-ui/elements/badge'
  import '@caderno-ui/elements/card'
</script>
